From 29205518b855cc86ba500e11468917225247cecd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 16:02:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agents): patch data-loss bugs from Fable review
 (C2/C3/C4, P1/P2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Addresses the merge-blocking data-loss bugs found in the #311 review. Test-first
(RED→GREEN) for every fix.

C2 (data loss): mergeJsonMcp discarded the entire existing .mcp.json on any JSON
parse error (JSONC comments/trailing commas Cursor tolerates), wiping user servers.
Now throws McpConfigParseError; renderMcpConfig backs the file up to a numbered
.bak and leaves it UNTOUCHED (never overwrites). Test: malformed-but-populated
config → servers preserved + backed up + skipped.

C3 (data loss): setup destroyed a user's hand-authored .cursorrules with no backup.
New exported backupAndRemoveLegacyCursorRules() copies to .cursorrules.bak (numbered
.bak.N on repeat) before removal, mirroring the AGENTS.md markerless backup. Test:
existing .cursorrules → backed up, not lost.

C4 (drift persists on upgrade): renderRulesForHarness skipped ALL existing .mdc, so a
stale Forge-managed rule survived `forge setup` forever. Now Forge-managed generated
files (identified by the "Generated by Forge" marker) are refreshed even without
--overwrite; user-authored rules (no marker) are still never clobbered. Tests: stale
generated .mdc → refreshed; user .mdc → untouched.

P1 (contract): the frozen MCP descriptor could not represent an http server. Added
optional `url`; stdio→command/args, http→url (validateDescriptor enforces per
transport; toJsonServerEntry + Codex TOML emit url for http).

P2 (footgun): bin/forge.js held a stale, DEAD parallel setup copy (superseded by the
lib/commands/setup.js registry command, which returns before the inline block runs).
Removed the broken refs to the deleted .claude/rules/workflow.md (setupClaudeAgent +
copyAgentRules) and the now-unused readFile; banner marks the path legacy. Full
deletion of the ~2000-line dead subsystem deferred as disproportionately risky.

Regenerated the D20 kill-list artifact (setup.js line shifts).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
